```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: green
REAL_USE_CASE: Production RAG teams using Snowflake/snowflake-arctic-embed-s (or other models shipping non-empty prompts via config_sentence_transformers.json) with standard vector-DB wrappers (Chroma, Milvus/pymilvus, LangChain, LlamaIndex). When using the prod-DEFAULT DB integration path without manually specifying the query prompt, retrieval recall drops ~9-10pp R@10 vs the correct path that honors the shipped prompt. The failure survives a competent user who deliberately selected a self-describing model and used the standard DB integration, because the wrapper silently discards the artifact's prompt contract at the DB boundary.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win, not microbenchmark artifact. L0 (EXP-0072) on BEIR/SciFact (5183 docs / 300 queries, exact cosine NN, ST 5.5.1) shows +9.37pp R@10 (0.7292 → 0.8229), 95% paired-bootstrap CI [+6.3, +13.0]pp, 29/300 queries improved, 0 hurt, MRR 0.5701→0.6718. Alias-break control (C, prompt-on-docs-too) yields 0.8212 ~= B, confirming gain is from query receiving its trained prompt, not asymmetry artifact. Could-it-fail control (intfloat/e5-small-v2, ships no prompt) shows A==B==0.8129 exactly, effect vanishes — not a construction tautology. The win is retrieval quality, not speed; +9pp recall directly translates to better downstream RAG answers in production. Survives realistic deployment because the seam is in the embedding contract, not the search kernel.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [1] All 4 source-verified production wrappers (Chroma SentenceTransformerEmbeddingFunction, pymilvus SentenceTransformerEmbeddingFunction, LangChain HuggingFaceEmbeddings, LlamaIndex HuggingFaceEmbedding) currently discard the shipped prompt (verified 2026-06-04, GitHub live). None auto-load from config_sentence_transformers.json. [2] Fix requires upstream wrapper changes to auto-read the artifact's prompt fields, or users must manually configure query_instruction/prompt in wrapper init. [3] Only models shipping non-empty prompts are affected (Snowflake arctic does; e5-small-v2 does not). [4] If a wrapper already auto-honors (none of the 4 do) or model ships empty prompt, gap vanishes — actionable negative result.
RATIONALE: The seam is open in production tooling (4 wrappers source-verified), the effect size is operationally meaningful for RAG (+9pp R@10 is substantial; 29 queries improved, 0 hurt), and the controls validate the mechanism (alias-break holds, could-it-fail holds). The product pain is real: a competent user selecting a self-describing model (ST v3+ auto-applies via encode_query) and using the standard DB integration will silently get degraded retrieval, with no warning from the wrapper. The negative result is actionable: check if your model ships a prompt (config_sentence_transformers.json exists and non-empty) and if your wrapper honors it; if not, manually configure or await wrapper fix. Citation: L0 EXP-0072 (independent reproduction, honest R@1 caveat noted), source-verification of 4 wrappers (2026-06-04), prior-art E5/Wang2022 and Instructor/TART (prompts help, not re-derived), MTEB PR#1221 (Aug 2024, benchmark lag).
```
